From 310e66ed75c34da9336eb48123b14aaa795233a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 20:40:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] DVHdr10PlusFill: one source for each scene of HDR10+ sent as
 Dolby Vision

A picture of HDR10+ sent as Dolby Vision whose HDR10+ metadata give no level 1
block, or that has none (credits, a stream that leaves them out), went out with
the metadata of the last scene that had them, as a repeated RPU: twelve in a
row and the stream went to the ordinary output, so the display left Dolby
Vision, and came back 48 or more pictures after the statistics did.

CDVHdr10PlusFill decides, per picture as it is presented, what goes out, with
one source for each scene so that the display's mapping never changes source
in the middle of a shot:

- a scene of the stream's own statistics: the decoder's metadata, as before;
  the first picture after measured ones carries a scene refresh;
- a scene of HDR10+ metadata without statistics: measured from its first
  picture, which is where its HDR10+ metadata say that a scene starts; the
  measurement is asked to start a scene there;
- pictures without HDR10+ metadata, which have no cuts of their own: in a
  scene of HDR10+ metadata they keep its metadata (a gap in a shot) until the
  measurement finds a scene cut, where it takes over; after measured pictures,
  or before any scene, they are measured.

Within a measured scene the level 1 block is what the measurement sends, cuts
and steps as for HDR10 measured as Dolby Vision. A picture of a measured scene
of which nothing is measured yet keeps the level 1 block that went out last,
with the scene's refresh. A refresh of the measurement that is the start it
was asked for (also one of a picture measured after its presentation) is no
cut it found.

The class only decides, so that a host test runs it with the module's own
decisions; the window system calls it in the commit after this one.
---
 xbmc/windowing/gbm/DVHdr10PlusFill.h | 279 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 279 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 xbmc/windowing/gbm/DVHdr10PlusFill.h

diff --git a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/DVHdr10PlusFill.h b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/DVHdr10PlusFill.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..728439b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/DVHdr10PlusFill.h
@@ -0,0 +1,279 @@
